{"id":2163,"date":"2025-05-15T11:00:00","date_gmt":"2025-05-15T16:00:00","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/?post_type=news&#038;p=2163"},"modified":"2025-05-15T11:09:51","modified_gmt":"2025-05-15T16:09:51","slug":"horror-movie","status":"publish","type":"news","link":"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/news\/horror-movie\/","title":{"rendered":"Horror Movie"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-lights-camera-action\"><em>Lights, camera, action!<\/em><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>It\u2019s the golden age of silent filmmaking, with instant classics popping up on the silver screen left and right. But when an ambitious new producer unwittingly releases accursed horrors upon three different film sets, it\u2019s up to our intrepid investigators to fix things before the credits roll on the entire production!<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Fantasy Flight Games is thrilled to announce the <em>Film Fatale<\/em> <em>Scenario Pack<\/em> for <em>Arkham Horror: The Card Game<\/em>!<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>In this showstopping scenario pack, one to four investigators ham it up at Hollywood\u2019s Lot C, where three troubled film sets are host to several bizarre and dangerous events. As with previous scenario packs, <em>Film Fatale<\/em> can be played standalone or inserted into a campaign as a side-story. With multiple ways the scenario can play depending on which movie set is the main feature, this is one blockbuster that will keep you coming back again and again.<\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/image-converter?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.svc.asmodee.net%2Fproduction-arkhamhorror%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F05%2FAHC85_Article_Announce_CarFan.png&amp;attachment_id=2167\" alt=\"Film Fatale card fan\" class=\"wp-image-2167\"\/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-quiet-on-set\"><strong>Quiet on Set<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Our story begins when silent film star Andr\u00e9 Patel (<em>Film Fatale<\/em>, 24) invites you and your fellow investigators to the grounds of Hollywood\u2019s Lot C. Ever since the producer, Erika Strand, brought some new props to the scene, strange things have been happening; cameras and equipment have gone missing, a series of accidents nearly halted production, and rumors spread about the films being \u201ccursed.\u201d No one took any of it seriously\u2026until a cast member was found dead on set. Now, with Andr\u00e9\u2019s help, it\u2019s up to your team to figure out which of the producer\u2019s new props is causing these bizarre events, and which of the lot\u2019s three film sets is most affected.<\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/image-converter?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.svc.asmodee.net%2Fproduction-arkhamhorror%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F05%2FAHC85_Article_Announce_Spread2_LotC.png&amp;attachment_id=2168\" alt=\"Movie lot exterior\" class=\"wp-image-2168\"\/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n<p>You start the day at the Central Lot (<em>Film Fatale<\/em>, 8a), where you\u2019ll need to spend clues to figure out which prop is the culprit. To find clues, you\u2019ll investigate the Space Set (<em>Film Fatale<\/em>, 9) of <em>A Cosmic Journey<\/em>, the Jungle Set (<em>Film Fatale<\/em>, 10) of <em>The Forgotten Island<\/em>, and the Gothic Set (<em>Film Fatale<\/em>, 11) of <em>The Abominable Contessa<\/em>. As you sift around the various sets, you\u2019ll have to contend with horrifying Found Footage (<em>Film Fatale<\/em>, 13), hazards that might Break a Leg (<em>Film Fatale<\/em>, 15), and persistent Possessed Extras (<em>Film Fatale<\/em>, 19). Just keep your cool, check things out, and watch out for when something tries to Flip the Script (<em>Film Fatale<\/em>, 12)!<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>When you figure out which prop is the one that\u2019s actually cursed, the story progresses to the second act. Unfortunately, by that point, things have gotten\u2026weird.<\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/image-converter?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.svc.asmodee.net%2Fproduction-arkhamhorror%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F05%2FAHC85_Article_Announce_Spread3_SaturniteMonarch.png&amp;attachment_id=2169\" alt=\"Reptilian bird creatures gathered around a table\" class=\"wp-image-2169\"\/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n<p>Depending on which prop ended up being the problem, you\u2019ll find yourselves whisked away into a strange world based on one of Lot C\u2019s current films\u2014or, perhaps more accurately, that movie\u2019s world has been warped into reality! For example, if you determine the cursed prop to be the Helios Telescope (<em>Film Fatale<\/em>, 5), then you\u2019ll find yourself within <em>A Cosmic Journey<\/em>, where the set has transformed into the far reaches of space. You\u2019ll have to battle alien Saturnites (<em>Film Fatale<\/em>, 33), try not to wind up lost on an Asteroid (<em>Film Fatale<\/em>, 34), and take cover from Celestial Showers (<em>Film Fatale<\/em>, 35) as you search the cosmos for the telescope\u2019s missing parts. Perhaps if you can parley with the Saturnite Monarch (<em>Film Fatale<\/em>, 32a), you can live long and prosper enough to make it back to Hollywood safe and sound.<\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/image-converter?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.svc.asmodee.net%2Fproduction-arkhamhorror%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F05%2FAHC85_Article_Announce_Spread4_Allosaurus.png&amp;attachment_id=2170\" alt=\"An allosaurus roaring\" class=\"wp-image-2170\"\/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n<p>If the cursed prop is the Staff of the Serpent (<em>Film Fatale, <\/em>6), then you\u2019ll be transported into the dinosaur-trodden world of <em>The Forgotten Island<\/em>. Arkham\u2019s investigators have dealt with dark cultists and unspeakable monsters in the past, but being chased down by a Dromaeosaurus (<em>Film Fatale<\/em>, 45) is certainly a new experience! It doesn\u2019t help that these Primordial Terrors (<em>Film Fatale<\/em>, 46) can pounce on you if you aren\u2019t prepared, and even your own assets can undergo an Unexpected Transformation (<em>Film Fatale<\/em>, 47) and bite the hand that wields them. As if that wasn\u2019t bad enough, you\u2019ll also have to evade a relentless Allosaurus (<em>Film Fatale<\/em>, 44a) constantly hunting you as you scour the jungle for your way back home. Objects in the mirror are closer than they appear, and you\u2019ll need some quick wits\u2014and quicker feet\u2014if you want to avoid becoming lunch!<\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/image-converter?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.svc.asmodee.net%2Fproduction-arkhamhorror%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F05%2FAHC85_Article_Announce_Spread5_TheContessa.png&amp;attachment_id=2171\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2171\"\/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n<p>Still, what\u2019s worse: becoming a dinosaur\u2019s lunch, or a vampire\u2019s dinner? If the Accursed Cape (<em>Film Fatale<\/em>, 7) is the cursed prop, you and your team will find yourselves invited to the banquet of <em>The Abominable Contessa<\/em>. It\u2019s an invitation you can\u2019t refuse, but you\u2019ll wish you could! The star of this show is The Contessa (<em>Film Fatale<\/em>, 55a) herself, who loves to poof in and out of investigators\u2019 locations like the horror movie monster she is. In order to escape her fiendish manor, you\u2019ll have to fend off her Vampire Thralls (<em>Film Fatale<\/em>, 56), dodge her burning Hellfire (<em>Film Fatale<\/em>, 58), and endure her deadly Vampire\u2019s Kiss (<em>Film Fatale<\/em>, 59). Life is preciously fragile in a horror story, and you\u2019ll have to pull out all the stops if you want to survive, lest these children of the night make music with your screams!<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-that-s-a-wrap\"><strong>That\u2019s a Wrap!<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>This is one you\u2019ll definitely want to see in theaters. By the time the credits roll on <em>Film Fatale<\/em>, you\u2019ll be left with an <em>Arkham Horror: The Card Game<\/em> experience you won\u2019t forget. Who knows, maybe you\u2019ll even want to make it a double feature and see how things play out differently the next time! Take your seats and look forward to this adventure through the silver screen when <em>Film Fatale<\/em> hits store shelves in August!<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><em>You can pre-order your copy of the <\/em>Film Fatale Scenario Pack <em>(AHC85) at your local retailer or <a href=\"https:\/\/www.fantasyflightgames.com\/en\/products\/arkham-horror-the-card-game\/products\/film-fatale\/\">online through our webstore<\/a> today!<\/em><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><em>Written by Peter Schumacher<\/em><\/p>\n","protected":false},"featured_media":2165,"parent":0,"template":"","meta":{"_acf_changed":true},"key-tag":[15,41],"class_list":["post-2163","news","type-news","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","key-tag-card-games","key-tag-ffg"],"acf":[],"yoast_head":"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO Premium plugin v22.3 (Yoast SEO v22.9) - https:\/\/yoast.com\/wordpress\/plugins\/seo\/ -->\n<title>Horror Movie | ArkhamHorror.com | The Official Arkham Horror Website News<\/title>\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\" \/>\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/news\/horror-movie\/\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Horror Movie | ArkhamHorror.com | The Official Arkham Horror Website News\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Announcing 